# CombatMode Architecture and Style

Ownership detail lives in **Lua file headers**. Load order: **`STRUCTURE.md`** + **`CombatMode/Embeds.xml`**. Prefer Blizzard APIs + `local _, CM = ...`; do **not** reintroduce Ace3/LibStub or `CombatMode/Libs/**` unless explicitly requested.

## Folder map

- `CombatMode/CombatMode.toc` — metadata, `SavedVariables: CombatModeDB`
- `CombatMode/Embeds.xml` — script load order + root frame `OnEvent` / `OnUpdate`
- `CombatMode/Constants/` — static tables (`Namespace.lua` first)
- `CombatMode/Core/{Runtime,FreeLook,Crosshair,ClickCasting,PartyRadial}/` — runtime by domain
- `CombatMode/UI/{Options,Changelog,Editors}/` — options toolkit/tabs, in-game changelog, secondary editors
- `CombatMode/Bindings.xml` — keybind declarations

## Watch-outs (read the file header for full ownership)

- **CVarManager** — all addon `SetCVar` writes; prior snapshot capture/restore; reticle presets + overrides; Interaction HUD SoftTarget subset.
- **FreeLookController** — mouselook lock/unlock; centering `0 → MouselookStart → deferred 1`; OPie rematch latch.
- **Crosshair companions** — Interaction HUD and Assisted Combat are separate modules; assist FlipBook/explode/break stay in `AssistedHighlight.lua`, not `Animations.lua` (reticle cast feedback only).
- **Options** — standalone `CombatModeOptionsFrame` (`CM.OpenOptions` / `/cm`), not Blizzard settings; tabs wire to existing `CM.*` + `CM.DB` only.

## Coding conventions

- Per-file global aliases only (no shared `CM.API` alias module). Header order: AddOn namespace (`local _, CM = ...`; Runtime uses `local addonName, CM = ...`) → WoW API → Lua stdlib → module locals. Do not use `local CM = _G.CM`.
- Centralize events via `Constants/Gameplay.lua` + `EventRouter`; no ad-hoc event frames.
- Extend existing `CM` APIs; keep DB scope intentional (`CM.DB.global` vs `CM.DB.char`).
- New settings → matching `UI/Options/Tabs/Tab*.lua` via `ctx:*` helpers + `CM.UI.Options.AddTab`.
- Preserve slash commands and keybinds unless explicitly changing them.
- Lint: `pwsh ./scripts/lint-changed.ps1` (full `pre-commit run --all-files` only for release / explicit request).

## Durable runtime notes

Record non-obvious fixes here (or in `combatmode-lua-safety.mdc`) — one place.

- **Root frame events:** `CombatMode_OnEvent(self, event, ...)` — first arg is the frame, not the event name.
- **DB shape:** AceDB-compatible (`CombatModeDB.global` + `char["Name - Realm"]`); defaults merge in `CM.InitDatabase`.
- **Cast feedback:** Animations outer `OnUpdate` (one motion); terminals via `CM.NotifyCrosshairCastTerminal`; gated by `crosshairCastFeedback`.
- **Assisted Combat matching:** short recent-suggestion cache — `GetNextCastSpell` often advances before `UNIT_SPELLCAST_SUCCEEDED`.
- **Options preview:** tab `onSelect`/`onDeselect`; Crosshair → `CM.SetCrosshairOptionsPreview`; Party Radial → `CM.PartyRadial.SetOptionsPreview` (layout-only). Do not reuse mouselook-gated Show/Hide.
- **Options theme:** monochrome via `UI.StripColors`; accent yellow only for headers, selected tab, toggle on-states.

## Change expectations

- Edit the owning module; keep headers accurate when ownership moves. Default header shape for every Lua file: What it does / Architecture / Does not / Related (see docs-sync rule).
- Call out behavior changes that affect mouselook, targeting CVars, or binding overrides.
